    "['remote-as [as_number] local-address [ip_address]', [{'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'peer 10.3.1.1 as-number 100', 'parent_command': ['user-group [parameter1]'], 'root': 'user-group [parameter1]', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': 'Here\\'s the translated HUAWEI equivalent command for the specified Juniper configuration:\\n\\n##\\npeer 10.3.1.1 as-number 100\\npeer 10.3.1.1 connect-interface 10.3.1.2\\n##\\n\\nNote: In HUAWEI devices, the BGP configuration is structured differently. The \"local-address\" functionality is achieved through the \"connect-interface\" parameter under the peer configuration, and the AS number is specified in a separate command. The IP address after \"connect-interface\" must be an address of a local interface (in this case, matching the Juniper configuration\\'s local-address parameter).', 'trans_template': 'peer 10.3.1.1 as-number 100'}, {'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'peer 10.3.1.1 connect-interface 10.3.1.2', 'parent_command': ['user-group [parameter1]'], 'root': 'user-group [parameter1]', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': 'Here\\'s the translated HUAWEI equivalent command for the specified Juniper configuration:\\n\\n##\\npeer 10.3.1.1 as-number 100\\npeer 10.3.1.1 connect-interface 10.3.1.2\\n##\\n\\nNote: In HUAWEI devices, the BGP configuration is structured differently. The \"local-address\" functionality is achieved through the \"connect-interface\" parameter under the peer configuration, and the AS number is specified in a separate command. The IP address after \"connect-interface\" must be an address of a local interface (in this case, matching the Juniper configuration\\'s local-address parameter).', 'trans_template': 'peer 10.3.1.1 connect-interface 10.3.1.2'}]]": 1,
    "['set protocols ospf area [area_id]', [{'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'ospf 1', 'parent_command': [], 'root': 'ospf 1', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': \"Here's the translated Huawei equivalent for the specified Juniper OSPF configuration commands:\\n\\n##\\nospf 1\\n area 0.0.0.0\\n  network 4.4.4.4 0.0.0.0\\n  network 10.4.1.0 0.0.0.255\\n##\\n\\nNotes:\\n1. In Huawei, OSPF is configured with a process ID (1 in this case) rather than direct area assignment\\n2. The 'passive' interface (lo0.1 in Juniper) is translated by advertising the loopback's exact address (4.4.4.4/32) with a 0.0.0.0 wildcard mask\\n3. The active interface (ge-2/0/0.0) is translated by advertising its network (10.4.1.0/24) with the appropriate wildcard mask\\n4. Huawei uses 'network' statements under the area instead of explicit interface declarations\", 'trans_template': 'ospf 1'}, {'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'area 0.0.0.0', 'parent_command': [], 'root': 'area 0.0.0.0', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': \"Here's the translated Huawei equivalent for the specified Juniper OSPF configuration commands:\\n\\n##\\nospf 1\\n area 0.0.0.0\\n  network 4.4.4.4 0.0.0.0\\n  network 10.4.1.0 0.0.0.255\\n##\\n\\nNotes:\\n1. In Huawei, OSPF is configured with a process ID (1 in this case) rather than direct area assignment\\n2. The 'passive' interface (lo0.1 in Juniper) is translated by advertising the loopback's exact address (4.4.4.4/32) with a 0.0.0.0 wildcard mask\\n3. The active interface (ge-2/0/0.0) is translated by advertising its network (10.4.1.0/24) with the appropriate wildcard mask\\n4. Huawei uses 'network' statements under the area instead of explicit interface declarations\", 'trans_template': 'area 0.0.0.0'}, {'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'network 4.4.4.4 0.0.0.0', 'parent_command': [], 'root': 'network 4.4.4.4 0.0.0.0', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': \"Here's the translated Huawei equivalent for the specified Juniper OSPF configuration commands:\\n\\n##\\nospf 1\\