    "['interface [interface_name]', [{'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'mpls enable', 'parent_command': ['ospf 1'], 'root': 'ospf 1', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': 'Here\\'s the equivalent Huawei configuration translation for the specified Juniper commands:\\n\\n##\\nmpls enable\\nmpls ldp enable\\ninterface GigabitEthernet2/0/0\\n ospf enable 1 area 0.0.0.0\\n##\\n\\nNote:\\n1. In Huawei, MPLS and LDP are enabled globally first, then activated on interfaces\\n2. The \"mpls enable\" command activates both MPLS forwarding and LDP if LDP is enabled globally\\n3. OSPF interface assignment uses the \"ospf enable <process-id> area <area>\" syntax\\n4. These commands assume proper global MPLS, LDP and OSPF configurations exist (equivalent to the Juniper global settings)', 'trans_template': 'mpls enable'}, {'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'mpls ldp enable', 'parent_command': [], 'root': 'mpls ldp enable', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': 'Here\\'s the equivalent Huawei configuration translation for the specified Juniper commands:\\n\\n##\\nmpls enable\\nmpls ldp enable\\ninterface GigabitEthernet2/0/0\\n ospf enable 1 area 0.0.0.0\\n##\\n\\nNote:\\n1. In Huawei, MPLS and LDP are enabled globally first, then activated on interfaces\\n2. The \"mpls enable\" command activates both MPLS forwarding and LDP if LDP is enabled globally\\n3. OSPF interface assignment uses the \"ospf enable <process-id> area <area>\" syntax\\n4. These commands assume proper global MPLS, LDP and OSPF configurations exist (equivalent to the Juniper global settings)', 'trans_template': 'mpls ldp enable'}, {'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'interface GigabitEthernet2/0/0', 'parent_command': ['ospf 1'], 'root': 'ospf 1', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': 'Here\\'s the equivalent Huawei configuration translation for the specified Juniper commands:\\n\\n##\\nmpls enable\\nmpls ldp enable\\ninterface GigabitEthernet2/0/0\\n ospf enable 1 area 0.0.0.0\\n##\\n\\nNote:\\n1. In Huawei, MPLS and LDP are